## Day 2: S3 Operations Deep Dive

### What I Did
- Created buckets in multiple regions (us-east-1, eu-west-1, ap-south-1)
- Used `aws s3 sync` to upload entire folder structures
- Deleted individual files and entire buckets
- Enabled S3 versioning and observed multiple file versions

### New Commands Learned
```bash
aws s3 sync &lt;local&gt; &lt;s3://bucket/&gt;          # Recursive upload
aws s3 rm s3://bucket/file.txt              # Delete single file
aws s3 rm s3://bucket/ --recursive          # Empty bucket
aws s3 rb s3://bucket                       # Delete bucket
aws s3api put-bucket-versioning             # Enable versioning
aws s3api list-object-versions              # View all versions
